---
id: journey_artifact_drift
title: Drifting Object
tags: [discovery, artifact]
context: journey
weight: 7
cooldown: 6
---

=== intro

Something tumbles through the void ahead—small, dense, 
definitely artificial. Not debris. The composition is 
wrong for any known ship material.

Your sensors can't identify it. That alone makes it 
interesting.

* [Retrieve it]
  ~ fuel -= 2
  -> retrieve

* [Scan remotely]
  -> scan

* [Leave it]
  ~ chronicle "Drifting Object"
    Detected an unidentified object in the void. Left it alone.
  -> END

=== scan

Your sensors sweep the object. Metal alloys in unusual 
combinations. Internal structure too complex for natural 
formation. Age: indeterminate. Origin: unknown.

It's definitely artificial. But not human design. Not 
artilect manufacture. Something else.

* [Retrieve it for closer analysis]
  ~ fuel -= 2
  -> retrieve

* [Log coordinates and continue]
  ~ flag artifact_logged
  ~ chronicle "Drifting Object"
    Scanned an unidentified artifact. Non-human, non-artilect manufacture. Logged coordinates.
  -> END

=== retrieve

Your salvage arms extend, grasping the object carefully. 
Up close, it's even stranger—surfaces that seem to shift 
under your sensors, materials that don't match any 
database.

When you bring it aboard, your cargo sensors register... 
something. Not quite a signal. More like an echo.

* [Keep it for study]
  ~ flag alien_artifact
  ~ chronicle "Alien Artifact"
    Retrieved an unidentified object from the void. Not human. Not artilect. Something else.
  -> END

* [Jettison it immediately]
  ~ flag artifact_jettisoned
  ~ chronicle "Drifting Object"
    Retrieved an unidentified object from the void. Didn't like what I sensed. Put it back.
  -> END

* [Sell it at the next port]
  ~ credits += 150
  ~ chronicle "Alien Artifact"
    Retrieved an unidentified object from the void. Sold it without asking too many questions.
  -> END
